! Case 2: linear, collisionless, kinetic ions AND electrons, ELECTROSTATIC.
! W7-X, one field period along alpha0 = 0, zonal mode at kx rho = 0.2,
! initialised as a zonal charge perturbation (ginit_option = 'rh').
!
! This case exists because the electromagnetic multi-species case next to it
! fails and a single case could not say which of its two new ingredients was
! responsible.  Turning the fields off while keeping the second species is
! meant to answer it.  It is also the cheapest case that can see a per-species
! normalisation error at all: with one species at m = T = 1 a wrong power of
! sqrt(T/m) and the right one are the same number; with kinetic electrons they
! differ by 61.  That is what the momentum inertia bug turned out to be.
!
! The setup is case 1's -- one field period, nzed 128, nvgrid 48, nmu 24,
! delt 0.05, nstep 2000, den0 = upar0 = 1 -- with two changes, both forced.
!
! The initial condition.  ginit_option = 'rh', not 'default'.  'default' puts
! the same density and parallel-flow perturbation into every species.  With
! adiabatic electrons that is a zonal charge perturbation, and case 1 is
! initialised that way; with kinetic electrons it is a NEUTRAL one, and the
! zonal flow is only its polarisation residual: Phi_i(0) = 0.27(1+i) as in
! case 1 against Phi_e(0) = -0.29(1+i), 94% cancelled, E_RH(0) = 1.0e-02
! against 1.1 for case 1 with the same g_i.  The drift then acts on the
! neutral part of g, which the zonal-flow energy does not see, and E_RH grows
! through the run instead of relaxing.  The budget did close on that state
! (4.6e-02 at nfield_periods = 2, both species on dPhi/dt = -i kx F to 1%),
! but what it measured was a 6% remainder of two cancelling projections: on a
! longer tube (nfield_periods = 4) the electron projection came off its drift
! by 7x while the ion held to 20%, and the flow turned over only 0.43 times
! in the suite's window, so the case would not have been asserted at all.
! 'rh' weights the density perturbation by Z_s, so the two species carry the
! same zonal charge, Phi_i(0) = 0.058 and Phi_e(0) = 0.060 add, and the flow
! relaxes at P/2E = -5.4e-03 at t = 30 -- the same rate as case 1 on this
! tube, -4.4e-03, as it should be for an ion-scale zonal flow.  The parallel
! flow upar0 = 1 is kept for symmetry with case 1; without it the residual is
! 9.3e-02 instead of 9.0e-02.
!
! The field line.  alpha0 = 0, not the 0.7 of the other W7-X decks, because
! with kinetic electrons and no collisions the zonal mode on the alpha0 = 0.7
! tube is numerically unstable and the budget cannot be measured at all.  A
! W7-X flux tube along alpha0 = 0.7 does not close on itself, and the zonal
! mode is periodic in z regardless: at the join the coefficients jump (one
! field period: B 1.037 -> 1.026, gds22 0.0079 -> 0.0342, gbdrift0 +0.0029 ->
! -0.0212, b.grad z -0.449 -> -0.467).  With adiabatic electrons that costs
! the odd invariant its conservation (case 1) and nothing more.  With kinetic
! electrons the zonal mode grows exponentially: |phi|^2 goes from 0.107 to
! 2.7e+05 by t = 300 at nfield_periods = 8 (amplitude growth rate 0.025) and
! to 7e+11 by t = 100 at nfield_periods = 1 (0.145); with 'rh' in place of
! 'default' the rates are 0.026 and 0.147.  The suite's old reading of this
! deck -- phi_RH residual 1.7e+01, Omega_RH 1.1e+03, electron projection off
! by 48x -- was that growth, not the diagnostic.
!
! The growth is not in any one operator and is not a resolved mode.  It
! survives xdriftknob = 0 (0.029 at nfp 8), include_mirror = .false. (0.047),
! mirror_semi_lagrange = .false., drifts_implicit = .false. and upwinding of
! 0.2 in z, vpa and t; it gets FASTER when the time step is halved (0.145 ->
! 0.92), when the velocity grid is refined (the electron projection error
! 47.6 -> 79.2 at 3x nvgrid) and at longer wavelength (0.84 at kx rho = 0.05,
! ~0.1 at 0.5 and 1.0); it is 0.31 at m_e = 1e-2.  It is absent with adiabatic
! electrons on the same tube (case 1 closes at 2.5e-02 there), absent with
! collisions (case 5, nu_e = 12, closes at 1.7e-02), and absent at alpha0 = 0,
! the stellarator-symmetric line, on which B, gds22 and b.grad z match across
! the join and the odd coefficients gbdrift0 and gds21 are antisymmetric:
! there |phi|^2 decays (rate -0.002) and at xdriftknob = 0 both projections
! hold to 5e-04 over t = 75.  Cases 3, 6, 9 and 10 in W7-X share the tube and
! the electrons; case 3 at alpha0 = 0 no longer grows but still fails on its
! dApar transient (see its deck).
!
! Tube length and tolerance.  alpha0 = 0 makes the transit-averaged drift of
! every passing particle vanish, so the drive is trapped particles alone and
! the odd invariant is not driven at all: Omega_RH turns over 0.01 times and
! is vacuous here, as it is in Miller.  The phi_RH residual is the parallel
! discretisation error known from case 1, which on this tube reads 0.13 for
! case 1 and 9.0e-02 here (|z| = 1.12 ion, 0.90 electron); at nzed 256 and
! nvgrid 96 they go to 0.091 and 6.2e-02 (1.08, 0.97), and neither moves with
! delt (nfield_periods = 2: 0.176 at delt 0.05 and 0.025, 0.113 at the finer
! grid).  Two field periods are worse, 0.176, as for case 1 (0.25).  The
! tolerance is 0.12 rather than case 1's 0.08 because case 1 gets its 0.08 on
! alpha0 = 0.7, where passing particles carry most of the drive, and that line
! is not available here.
!
! Miller is linear, collisionless and axisymmetric here, so every flux channel
! is identically zero and the budget reduces to the statement that the RH
! projection does not move at all.
&parameters_physics
  nonlinear = .false.
  vnew_ref = 0.1
  include_apar = .false.
  include_bpar = .false.
  beta = 0.0
/
&kt_grids_knobs
  grid_option = 'range'
/
&kt_grids_range_parameters
  naky = 1
  aky_min = 0.0
  akx_min = 0.2
  nakx = 1
/
&init_g_knobs
  ginit_option = 'rh'
  phiinit = 1.0
  den0 = 1.0
  upar0 = 1.0
  width0 = 1.0
/
&species_knobs
  nspec = 2
/
&species_parameters_1
  dens = 1.0
  fprim = 0.0
  mass = 1.0
  temp = 1.0
  tprim = 0.0
  type = 'ion'
  z = 1.0
/
&species_parameters_2
  dens = 1.0
  fprim = 2.2
  mass = 2.7e-4
  temp = 1.0
  tprim = 8.0
  type = 'electron'
  z = -1.0
/
&zgrid_parameters
  boundary_option = 'unconnected'
  nperiod = 1
  nzed = 128
/
&vpamu_grids_parameters
  nmu = 24
  nvgrid = 48
/
&knobs
  delt = 0.05
  nstep = 2000
  print_extra_info_to_terminal = .false.
  drifts_implicit = .true.
/
&stella_diagnostics_knobs
  nsave = -1
  nwrite = 1
  save_for_restart = .false.
  write_RH_integrands = .false.
  write_RH_inertia_fluxes = .true.
/
&geo_knobs
  geo_option = 'vmec'
/
&vmec_parameters
  nfield_periods = 1
  torflux = 0.5
  alpha0 = 0.0
  vmec_filename = 'wout_w7x_standard.nc'
/
&dissipation
  include_collisions = .false.
  collision_model = 'dougherty'
  hyper_dissipation = .false.
/
